From 4cc6e6ab81c9c1ffdc0d3413b6c4f5fde57efb55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:40:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: add tile_resolve and stitch_passes experiments
 (WIP)

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=tile_resolve compiles a tile-function variant of
custom-resolve fragment shaders that read only colour input
attachments. Input attachment reads become imageblock sample reads and
colour outputs become texture writes to the resolve images. In the final
segment of a multisampled custom-resolve pass, the custom resolve then
runs as a tile dispatch inside the same Metal render pass. Tile
pipelines are built per pass sample count on first use. By-region
fragment barriers in that segment are deferred and dropped if the
resolve follows. Transient MSAA colour with a don't-care store op is not
stored once resolved. The multiview whole-framebuffer check compares
against the attachments' layer counts.

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=stitch_passes creates suspending and resuming
render encoders for suspended and resumed dynamic rendering, commits the
joined command buffers together, ends the Metal command buffer after a
final resumed pass and commits the rest separately, and defers command
buffers submitted between the segments. Suspending encoders do not
store. Probes pass, but Alyx currently hits GPU timeouts with it.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

